    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157-a1">

                <pb facs="0343" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg303"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 3, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir:</hi> Viscount Monk informs me, by
                    telegraph, that the Canadian courts had decided that the St. Albans raiders
                    could not be surrendered, and they were consequently discharged.</p>
                <p>It appears, however, that the governor general directed their immediate re-arrest
                    on a charge of violating the Queen’s neutrality.</p>
                <p>Believe me to remain, my dear sir, yours very faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
